@meeting train.p3.calder
// Pillar 5, P3 (Day 5, Friday afternoon, after your second scanner reading): your first head-scratcher, at the board.
// Washer 2 leaks; the crew tried a door seal and a drain valve. Calder opens Fault notes with you and reads the first
// note; then she follows you. Head writer, seat W. The note's name is whoever really fitted it (the game's).
title: A funny one
from: Chief Ines Calder
gist: Your first head-scratcher: a washer that leaks. Notes from the crew say what's been tried. Cross off what didn't work.
== lines
calder: Here's a funny one. Washer 2 in the junior laundry. It leaks.   [gesture]
calder: Two people have had a go. Neither fixed it. Both left notes.
calder > you: Open Fault notes. Three suspects. The door seal, the drain valve, the pump.
calder: Rule one, page one. If someone fitted it and it's still wrong, it isn't that.
calder: First note's on the job. New door seal in. Still leaks. So?
? choice
* So it's not the seal.   rel:calder+2 flavour:practical
  calder: Cross it off.   [nod]
* Could the new seal be faulty?   rel:calder+1 flavour:listen
  calder: Could be. Isn't. Trust the note. Cross it off.
* (Tap the door seal)
  calder: Good. Crossed off.
calder: The other note's on the washer. Go and find it. I'll follow.
